I can’t push files from here, but I prepared a single, copy‑pasteable shell script that will create every scaffold file, commit them on branch loviora/mvp, push to GitHub and open the Pull Request (it uses the GitHub CLI for PR creation). Run this locally on a machine that has git and the GitHub CLI (gh) installed and authenticated.

How to run
1. Save the script below into a file named push_loviora_full.sh on your machine.
2. Make it executable:
   chmod +x push_loviora_full.sh
3. Run it:
   ./push_loviora_full.sh

Notes / prerequisites
- You must have git and gh installed and gh authenticated (gh auth login).
- The script clones your repo https://github.com/yoxyoxdur135-png/pulse.git — make sure that's the repo you want to update.
- The script will create branch loviora/mvp (or switch to it if it exists), write/overwrite files listed below, commit and push.
- The PR will be created from loviora/mvp → main using gh. If you don't have gh, the script will still push the branch and instruct how to create the PR manually.
- After the PR is created, rotate secrets (JWT_SECRET, DB passwords) before using in any external environment.
- If you prefer, run the script in a disposable environment and inspect changes before merging.

